{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1491484-the-book-of-alternatives-a-suggestion","id":1491484,"title":"The Book of Alternatives: a suggestion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-27T09:49:44-07:00","id":1491484,"title":"The Book of Alternatives: a suggestion","content":"The idea is simple. Create alternative forms of the major splats to fit the worlds/continuities of each major game line.<br /> <br /> Vampires as the get of a Farmer cursed by the Abrahamic God doesn't really work for the other games. I could see Vampires as a particularly free-willed sort of fomori in the Werewolf games. Or an exotic type of Risen in Wraith or Mage. As fairy vampires are already part of folklore that becomes obvious for Changeling.<br /> <br /> With a few rule changes to boost their power and flexibility, Sorcerers could replace Mages for the other games. Or the rules from the old Hunter: the Reckoning could be used. H:tR did their own Mages with Seven Spheres. <br /> <br /> In any case it would make crossovers more fluid and less of a challenge to each game's core idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-28-2022, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T11:38:57-07:00","id":1491503,"title":"","content":"I think Mages can work fine with their own rules if you simply add that the paradigms (lowercase) of the main gameline used are directly true, so they're Earthly Foundations and/or personal Paradigms must defer to them. And you can then add bits based on that, the ST may place any limitation or effect based on the &quot;actual paradigm of the world&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other than that I'll post later. I do need some ideas for this for my current Changeling game as the other splats are a big thing in the coming stories, and they're meant in this game to be, indeed, Prodigals (fae in origin if not in rules).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T12:47:31-07:00","id":1491512,"title":"","content":"The rules for Devil-Eaten (essentially Infernalist versions of Fomori/Possessed) from the revised Book of Madness were specifically designed so you could create vampires, werewolves, and other creatures with them. It's probably pretty easy to adapt them into modern Bygones as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T01:03:38-07:00","id":1491563,"title":"","content":"VAMPIRE<br /> <br /> Vampires are not the only ones with the Beast Within. Trauma in the face of death can awaken the Beast even in the living, but whereas the flesh of the dead stays dead and unchanging, the flesh of the living turns on itself and warps into animalistic forms. Hence the so-called <b>Changing Breeds</b> are born, the most famous among them being the <b>Lupines</b>, for wolves and dogs are kin closest to the Beast.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous power can be found within the Blood, as several Kindred Clans and Caitiff Bloodlines can well attest to. This magic of Blood is the magic of payment, and vampires pay the price with stolen life-power. The living can pay the price too, but they must make do with sacrifices of animals (including humans) and destruction of valuables. Every once in a while, such a sorcerer becomes <b>Awakened</b> to deeper laws of sorcery, channeling the World\u2019s own quintessential life-force to pay the Blood-price.<br /> <br /> Hmm, how should I do the others\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Refined 08-28-2022, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T15:49:48-07:00","id":1491667,"title":"","content":"I suspect that with Changeling, it would be fairly easy to make Vampyr and Wolfen Kiths to cover the traditional European concept of the two. Maybe also a Phantasm Kith for ghosts. <br /> <br /> With magic users, you could borrow a concept from Ars Magica in which the Fae realm is one of the four Realms of Power humans can obtain mystical power from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T17:57:52-07:00","id":1492257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1491484-the-book-of-alternatives-a-suggestion?p=1491667#post1491667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that with Changeling, it would be fairly easy to make Vampyr and Wolfen Kiths to cover the traditional European concepts .</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood drinking fairies are common enough. We've got several kiths that turn into animal forms. The Beastie, a type of Thailin, would require few changes to fit. Having a type of Fae magician that keeps magical powers but loses who they really are might fit the bill. As for Wraiths, perhaps a type of Chimera that could contact individuals not connected to the dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-03-2022, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T14:40:37-07:00","id":1492317,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about making the Prodigals a form of earlier attempts at the Changeling Way, Kiths (or maybe Gallain) that underwent some archaic method to attune to the Autumn World for some benefit, but at a cost that severed their connection to the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> My idea is to use their own normal rules, with just a few twists to make some of their traits be mutations of Glamour and Banality without their knowing, and changes in their settings so they have reason to keep their original lore, but it is actually Changeling in the end. One of my goals is that their weaknesses and curses will correlate to Banality and Bedlam.<br /> <br /> Finally, I want to make a &quot;merged state&quot; for each in case my players achieve some sort of &quot;return of the Prodigals&quot;. Nothing to complex, just a few changes in their standard templates to represent them recovering their basic fae natures without ceasing to be what they are. I may have some Kiths based on each splat, or even sub-splats, but those would be reserved for entities in the Deep Dreaming that never became Prodigals, are just related to the original ones. For those I would go full CtD rules and make them similar to Dark Kin.<br /> <br /> One such Dreaming entity could be Caine, or actually a number of legendary \u00dcber-Vampires, whose children and/or grand children came independently to the Autumn World and enacted their own form of possession, becoming the Antes and spreading their nightmare nature through the process of the Embrace. I'm still working out the details and thinking what is their link to the Redcaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T22:52:07-07:00","id":1492485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1491484-the-book-of-alternatives-a-suggestion?p=1491563#post1491563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VAMPIRE<br /> <br /> Vampires are not the only ones with the Beast Within. Trauma in the face of death can awaken the Beast even in the living, but whereas the flesh of the dead stays dead and unchanging, the flesh of the living turns on itself and warps into animalistic forms. Hence the so-called <b>Changing Breeds</b> are born, the most famous among them being the <b>Lupines</b>, for wolves and dogs are kin closest to the Beast.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous power can be found within the Blood, as several Kindred Clans and Caitiff Bloodlines can well attest to. This magic of Blood is the magic of payment, and vampires pay the price with stolen life-power. The living can pay the price too, but they must make do with sacrifices of animals (including humans) and destruction of valuables. Every once in a while, such a sorcerer becomes <b>Awakened</b> to deeper laws of sorcery, channeling the World\u2019s own quintessential life-force to pay the Blood-price.<br /> <br /> Hmm, how should I do the others\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>VAMPIRE (CONTINUED)<br /> <br /> <b>Spirits</b> exist as their own thing, but they are no more holy than what mortals and others (including themselves) account for. Each spirit is characterized by their intangibility, dominion over certain concepts, and most importantly, warping of space-time in their lairs and sanctums (a quality some occultists liken to the inevitable societal corruption caused by vampires). The most powerful ones can manifest pocket-worlds where they hold court as barons and kings, this being the truth of the &quot;Umbra&quot; that spiritualists and sorcerers speak of.<br /> <br /> Of manifold spirits, the <b>spirits of the dead</b> hold a special place, as their world-shaping relies on communal culture they followed in life, instead of personal prowess. Thus the Underworld is considered distinct from the shadows, its Dark Kingdoms a grisly and anachronistic facade of mortal history. And the Kingdoms' people? <b>Wraiths</b> struggle in angst over their Humanity, oblivious to the simple fact that emotions are only a substitute to what their shadowy Beasts truly crave for. <b>Specters</b> have given up their Humanity, and while most are nothing but Wights without a body, some have found Enlightenment within the Tempestuous Abyss to retain their sapience. Clan Cappadocius studies the former, promising anchors to the living world, even if the anchors are chains. Clan Lasombra mingles with the latter, luring them with flashes of raw life they may prey upon, while cracking open their minds to peek into the Deep Dark.<br /> <br /> Because spirits are both the Stranger and the Neighbor, some vampires have attempted to Embrace or Ghoul them as they would mortals. The results are usually singular, messy, or singularly messy. In the distant past however, a vampire or several dozens of them (rumored to be of Clan Ravnos, or Clan Malkavia) have successfully Embraced several elder spirits of dreams and stories, incarnating them in physical bodies. The Blood they feed upon is not of the body, but of the mind and raw soul-stuff. They do not Embrace, but inject their entire spirit into the hapless mortal; a reincarnation enabled by reverse-Diablerie. They call themselves <b>Kithain</b> and not Kindred, but nevertheless are kith-and-kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T21:58:32-07:00","id":1492864,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite takes on the vampire, for its novelty, comes from the Buffy the Vampire series. More focused on fighting demons than vampires, the show had it as canon that the curse of the vampire is a demonic possession of the soulless corpse. The notion makes the similarities between vampiric disciplines and Fallen lores make sense...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}